SEARCHING:
Searching means finding whether a particular element exists in the array and finding its position

CODE:
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

int target = 30;

for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] == target) {
        System.out.println("Element found at index " + i);
        break;
    }
}


OUTPUT:
Element found at index 2
